PAI 4.0 for QFX5120-48T-6C (BCM84894 "blackfin" copper gearbox).

Read SAI_SWITCH_ATTR_SLAVE_MDIO_ADDR_LIST as a map list.

The attribute is declared sai_u8_list_t upstream, which caps a slave entry at
eight bits and so cannot describe an MDIO address space larger than 255. It is
redeclared sai_map_list_t by

  sonic-juniper: patches/sonic-sairedis-sai/0001-change-slave-mdio-atrr-type.patch

so that each entry carries a 32-bit key and value: the key is the logical SONiC
phy id and the value the physical MDIO address.

sairedis serialises the attribute according to that declaration, so PAI has to
read the same shape. Left reading u8list it walks the sai_map_t array as raw
bytes and derives nonsense addresses -- on QFX5120 the first slave of the
0x0 domain came out as MDIO 48, and the broadcast core reset then failed with
"Invalid PHY".

Widen brcm_slave_phyid_list_t to uint32_t for the same reason the attribute was
widened, and take the address from the map value in the create path and return
it there in the get path.

